    "lawCode": "Rpld §368-b, amd §368-b, Exec L (as proposed in S.8729 & A.9590); add §29-a, Veterans' Services L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S854\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to authorizing public\nrequests for information from any county, city, town, or village desir-\ning to have any memorial located within their municipality listed within\nthe veterans memorial registry; to amend the veterans' services law, in\nrelation to directing the department of veterans' services to establish\na veterans memorial registry; and to repeal section 368-b of the execu-\ntive law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of\nL.2022,c., 588 relating to establishing a veterans memorial registry.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by including language\nthat would allow the searchable database to only consist of veteran\nmemorials that are submitted to the division. The state director must\nissue on behalf of the division a public request for information from\nany county, city, town or village that desires to have a memorial\nlocated in their municipality to be included in the registry. Any coun-\nty, city, town or village may submit a response to the division's\nrequest. Individuals and organizations may provide recommendations to\nmunicipalities to be included in the memorial registry. If a munici-\npality chooses to respond to the division's public request for informa-\ntion, it must identify the memorial(s) it desires to be included in the\nregistry and submit any required information. This legislation also\namended the underlying chapter by adding language to recognize the shift\nfrom the Division of Veterans Services to a Department.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 588 of the Laws of 2022. 5.8729 passed the\nSenate in May 2022 and A.9590 passed the Assembly in March 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the executive law relating to\ndirecting the division of veterans' services to develop a veterans memo-\nrial registry, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.8729 and\nA.9590, takes effect; provided, however, that section three of this act\nshall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as section 2\nof part PP of chapter 56 of the laws of 2022, takes effect.  Provided,\nfurther: (a) that the amendments made to subdivisions 2 and 3 of section\n368-b of the executive law made by section one of this act shall not\naffect the repeal of such section and shall be deemed repealed there-\nwith; and (b) that if section 2 of part PP of chapter 56 of the laws of\n2022 shall not have taken effect on or before such date then section two\nof this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\nsection 2 of part PP of chapter 56 of the laws of 2022, takes effect\n",
